From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:16:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 092/167] hjviewer: the controller says why a PC ended its
 password-less connection (TV-W5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W5 (design w5.md 3-2, 5-4; critic 2-5): a 1.9.0 PC that ends a
password-less connection sends a Korean close reason with a mark, "(login
ended, not allowed)" or "(password-less ended, not allowed)". The controller
shows, in place of the whole text, "이 기기의 로그인이 끝나 연결을 끊었습니다." /
"This device's login has ended, so the connection was closed." or "이 PC가
비밀번호 없는 연결을 더 받지 않아 연결을 끊었습니다." / "This PC no longer takes
password-less connections, so the connection was closed." (hjvSessionCutText,
hooked in handleMsgBox around hjvAccessMsgboxText through
hjvAccountMsgboxText). The core decides the reconnect on the text as it came,
so the "not allowed" still stops it; a text without a mark shows as before.

U1-d made honest: logging another device out says that its open
password-less connections end within a few minutes (the logout questions),
and the results say where they stay: "열려 있던 비밀번호 없는 연결은 PC가 서버에
닿으면 5분 안에 끊깁니다. PC가 서버에 닿지 못하거나 HJViewer 1.9.0 전 버전이면
남으니, …" (openSessions, w5.md 3-2; the verb is U32's "로그아웃하면"). The
"log out all other devices" question keeps its title as the question, so its
text keeps "지금 쓰는 이 기기는 로그인한 채로 둡니다." and takes W5's ending.

Tests: hjviewer_account_test.dart, the two marks in both languages, a mark in
another text, texts without one; the logout questions and results.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
